summary.text:
We need answer only JSON object with declaration, implementation, supporting_objects. Need implement FB_Task CODESYS ST. Need exact interface. Need reason behavior, edge toggles, modes, estop. Need include supporting DUTs referenced. We can define enum for phase as DUT. declaration is FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task followed by VAR sections; omit END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. implementation ST body alone. supporting_objects list helper DUT/POU each name kind declaration implementation; functions need return_type. Need no markdown.

Need craft valid CODESYS 3.5 ST. Need ensure declaration includes inputs/outputs and internal vars. Must define phase enum maybe E_Phase. Could use internal enum in VAR but supporting DUT required if referenced DUT. We can define E_PUB015_Phase. Need include phase variable perhaps as internal q. Initial_conditions mention phase IDLE, but not interface. We can have VAR phase : E_PUB015_Phase := E_PUB015_Phase.IDLE; and edge histories BOOL. Need handle mode changes clear latches sequence. Need edge history update during estop so held buttons cannot restart outputs on recovery. Need manual toggles: independent toggles for A/B/C/D/mixMotor in manual only when estop true and opeMode false, rising edge of each start. In manual, if estop false, all outputs off and latches reset. Edge histories should update every scan regardless of state? Assumption: Edge history updates during emergency stop so held buttons cannot restart outputs on recovery. Also edge history updates mode changes? likely yes. Need rising edge detection: use current input AND NOT prev. Then update prev at end every call.

Need automatic mode: autoStart rising edge accepted in IDLE. On start set phase FILL_A. Then same scan output? Tests: step autoStart true from IDLE expected valveARun true same observed scan. So when autoStart edge in auto and safe and phase IDLE, set phase FILL_A; output logic based on resulting phase should show A true. We can process transition then outputs.

Threshold transitions: one logical phase transition per invocation. But possible level already above threshold on start? At autoStart current level maybe 0. But if autoStart with level >=50, should start fill A then possibly threshold transition? "One logical phase transition per invocation" and toB pre-phase FILL_A. If new start sets FILL_A not pre-phase? To avoid transition same scan? likely no: autoStart sets FILL_A and outputs A regardless level? Need consider tests not. We can design transitions before autoStart? We should follow state based on pre-phase. autoStart only in IDLE. For start same scan, phase becomes FILL_A; if we do threshold transition after autoStart, could immediately go B if level >=50. Is that okay? "first opening valve A" but if level already high maybe transition. Not tested. One transition per invocation. Fine.

Need sequence:
IDLE -> on rising autoStart and safe and opeMode true, phase=FILL_A (valve A).
FILL_A: if levelSensor >=50 -> FILL_B (close A open B) else stay.
FILL_B: if level >=80:
  if processMode false -> MIX (mix motor)
  if processMode true -> FILL_C (valve C)
FILL_C: if level >=100 -> MIX (start mix)
MIX: if mixMotorComplete -> DRAIN (open D); stop mix
DRAIN: stay open until estop or mode reset. auto process ended? "automatic process ends" but valve D stays open. Phase DRAIN. autoStart edge accepted only IDLE. EStop resets IDLE. Mode change resets IDLE. If processMode changes during batch stays fixed? Assumption processMode stays fixed during batch; but if input changes? We should not clear? "processMode stays fixed during the batch" could ignore changes? It says assumptions maybe tests don't change. We can use current processMode only at FILL_B. Maybe store processMode for batch? Could but not needed. Changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence. Need detect mode change opeMode != prevOpeMode. On change reset manual latches and phase to IDLE. Also clear outputs. Should edge histories? update current.

Emergency: estop false => all actuator outputs false, reset all manual latches, phase IDLE, and edge histories update so held buttons cannot restart on recovery. So at start if not estop, set outputs false and reset. Need still detect edges? We update prev histories at end. If estop false, manual toggles ignored. Good.

Manual mode: opeMode false. Should automatic phase reset when entering manual? "Changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence." If mode currently manual and remains, phase should IDLE. If opeMode false, we should reset phase to IDLE? At least outputs manual latches only. In manual mode, automatic state should not run. If transition from auto to manual, mode change clears phase. If initially manual, phase IDLE. We can in manual branch if not estop, reset phase IDLE and execute toggles. But if estop true and manual, also phase idle. Need automatic outputs off except manual latches. Manual latches independent. When opeMode false, output valves/mix = corresponding manual latches. Do not preserve auto phase. Could set phase IDLE every manual scan. That seems okay. But "independent manual toggles may coexist." yes.

Manual toggle rising edge on each button. Need detect all edges even in auto? For mode changes, if in auto and buttons held, then switch to manual with button held: should not toggle due to no rising on that scan? If prevButton true from auto, current true => no rising. If button pressed in auto, edge history updated, then switch manual while held no toggle. Good. Need update edge histories every scan. If user releases and presses after manual, toggles.

Need handle mode change. If opeMode changes, clear old latches and sequence. Suppose manual latches on, then opeMode false->true: clear manual latches phase IDLE. If auto phase active, opeMode true->false: clear phase and manual latches? "Changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence." So yes clear manual latches too. Need if mode change and estop? already estop resets. We can detect modeChanged := opeMode <> prevOpeMode at start before reset. Then if modeChanged reset. But if safe false also reset. If opeMode false manual, toggles? If modeChanged to manual and a start button rising same scan, should it toggle? Hmm "Changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence." Could then process manual toggle same scan. If mode changed to manual and button rising same scan, unclear. Likely okay to allow? But old latches cleared. Not tested. We can process after reset. For auto mode change to auto with autoStart rising same scan: should accept? "autoStart is rising edge accepted in IDLE"; mode change resets to IDLE then autoStart edge could start. Maybe okay. But if mode change true and autoStart held, prev autoStart maybe true from before, no edge. Fine.

Need output logic. Approach implement with if estop then reset outputs; elsif opeMode then auto sequence; else manual toggles. Need output assignments each scan. Need ensure automatic mode outputs reflect phase only and no manual latches. When entering auto, manual latches reset due mode change or we can ignore. If opeMode true, output based on phase. Need assign valveARun etc. In ST, can assign initially false then set. Use variables outputs directly.

Need avoid forgetting edge histories update. Use temp variables risingA etc computed at top: aRise := valveAStart AND NOT prevValveAStart; etc. Then at end update prev*. Since if estop false still update edges.

