    // Process threshold transitions based on current phase (could be after autoStart). Need one transition per invocation. We can use CASE with one branch and transitions. If autoStart sets FILL_A, then CASE FILL_A can transition same scan if level>=50. Is that "one logical transition"? It would be start transition and threshold transition same scan, arguably two. Maybe okay? To be strict, if autoStart accepted, should not threshold transition same scan. Could use flag didStart. But not necessary. Yet LTL maybe. Tests: autoStart step level 0. Fine. But if autoStart with level >=50, expected? No tests. To respect "first opening valve A" and one phase transition per invocation, maybe don't process threshold on start scan? We can avoid by IF riseAuto THEN phase=FILL_A ELSE CASE... END_IF. But if phase not IDLE, process. That means one transition per invocation (IDLE->FILL_A). Good. However if phase IDLE and no autoStart, no. Let's implement:
    IF phase = IDLE THEN
